# Trivy ignore list (image scans).
# Each entry MUST include: severity, justification, expiry-or-followup.
# Re-evaluate every time we bump caddy / dependencies.
#
# How to re-audit (no docker needed): read the dependency versions caddy pins
# in its own go.mod for the tag we build —
#   https://raw.githubusercontent.com/caddyserver/caddy/<CADDY_VERSION>/go.mod
# — then ask OSV whether that exact version is still affected:
#   POST https://api.osv.dev/v1/query {"package":{"name":"<mod>","ecosystem":"Go"},"version":"<ver>"}
# An empty result means caddy has moved past the fix and the entry below is
# dead weight; delete it. OSV and trivy's DB are not identical, so confirm on
# the next CI run — the docker-images job scans with exit-code 0 and prints the
# full HIGH/CRITICAL table.
#
# Caddy v2.11.7 (2026-10-06) cleared all six entries carried for v2.11.4.
# GO-2026-5932 (x/crypto/openpgp unmaintained) has no CVE/GHSA alias and is
# not reported by trivy.

# === caddy gobinary, frontend + panel images ==================================
#
# Caddy v2.11.7 pins x/net v0.59.0. Go 1.27.2 / x/net v0.60.0 (2026-10-08)
# fixed five HTTP/2 flaws (GO-2026-6603, -6610, -6611, -6612, -6617); trivy
# reports only CVE-2026-78669 at HIGH. Our image builds caddy with Go 1.27.2,
# so the stdlib copy is fixed; the x/net copy is not reachable:
#
#   * both Caddyfiles set `servers { protocols h1 }`, so caddy never calls
#     x/net `http2.ConfigureServer` and serves no HTTP/2 or h2c;
#   * `frontend/Caddyfile` proxies to a plain-HTTP unix socket, where the
#     x/net HTTP/2 transport is never negotiated;
#   * `frontend/Caddyfile.panel` proxies over TLS only to our own control
#     plane, the only peer that could send hostile SETTINGS frames.
#
# Followup: caddy master already has x/net v0.60.0 (caddyserver/caddy#8179);
# drop this entry once a caddy release after v2.11.7 ships with it.

CVE-2026-78669        # HIGH x/net v0.59.0 (fix 0.60.0) — HTTP/2 SETTINGS initial-window CPU DoS; caddy HTTP/2 server disabled (protocols h1), client side talks only to our own CP.
